cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you reference TruePad, please cite the repository and the exact commit or
  release you used. TruePad 3.0 is DEVELOPMENT software; the latest FORMAL release
  is TruePad 2.0.0.
title: "TruePad — authenticated one-time-pad key management (educational/research)"
abstract: >-
  TruePad is an educational and research implementation of authenticated
  one-time-pad key management. It enforces the software-enforceable one-time-use
  requirements (literal XOR OTP confidentiality, one-time Wegman-Carter
  authentication, durable burn-before-output consumption, attempt reservation,
  rollback witnesses, a TPM-anchored monotonic authority, and an operator-pinned
  root of trust) while explicitly separating the physical premises software cannot
  prove. It does NOT guarantee perfect secrecy as a product claim.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The TruePad project"
    website: "https://github.com/systemslibrarian/TruePad"
repository-code: "https://github.com/systemslibrarian/TruePad"
url: "https://github.com/systemslibrarian/TruePad"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: "3.0.0-dev.0"
keywords:
  - one-time pad
  - authenticated one-time pad
  - Wegman-Carter authentication
  - cryptography education
  - TPM rollback protection
  - post-quantum pad delivery
